IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `loa-dates`
IMPORT `loa-core`

-- Limitation of Actions Act 1936 (SA) -- THE SEAT OF THE PERSON BRINGING THE ACTION: the injured person, the person
-- abused as a child, the person defamed, the creditor, the beneficiary, the executor suing for an estate. Every question
-- is asked as that person would ask it, from facts that person can state; the court's judgments are asked as
-- conditions. The rules are in loa-core.l4; this module restates none of them.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Based on content from the South Australian Legislation website at 6 November 2026 (the current version,
-- 1.7.2021, as the register's unauthorised RTF). State of South Australia, CC BY 4.0. See SOURCE-LICENSE.md. BASELINE
-- ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `The questions of the person bringing the action`

-- Builds the core's record from the plain answers; every field is read by some rule.
GIVEN `my kind of action` IS A `Kind of action`,
      `the day it accrued` IS A DATE,
      `my injury remained latent` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the day I first knew of the injury` IS A DATE,
      `there was a later acknowledgment or payment` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the day of the last acknowledgment or payment` IS A DATE,
      `they were absent from the State` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `they have returned` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the day they returned` IS A DATE,
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE,
      `I was mentally incapable` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the day the incapacity began` IS A DATE,
      `the incapacity has ended` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the day the incapacity ended` IS A DATE,
      `it is for an estate` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the day of death` IS A DATE,
      `the day of the grant` IS A DATE,
      `a concerns notice was given` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the day of the concerns notice` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Limitation facts`
`the facts from my answers` `my kind of action` `the day it accrued` `my injury remained latent` `the day I first knew of the injury` `there was a later acknowledgment or payment` `the day of the last acknowledgment or payment` `they were absent from the State` `they have returned` `the day they returned` `my date of birth` `I was mentally incapable` `the day the incapacity began` `the incapacity has ended` `the day the incapacity ended` `it is for an estate` `the day of death` `the day of the grant` `a concerns notice was given` `the day of the concerns notice` MEANS
    `Limitation facts` WITH
        `the kind of action` IS `my kind of action`
        `the day the cause of action accrued` IS `the day it accrued`
        `the injury remained latent` IS `my injury remained latent`
        `the day the injury first came to the person's knowledge` IS `the day I first knew of the injury`
        `there was a later acknowledgment or payment` IS `there was a later acknowledgment or payment`
        `the day of the last acknowledgment or payment` IS `the day of the last acknowledgment or payment`
        `the person liable was absent from the State when it accrued` IS `they were absent from the State`
        `the person liable has returned to the State` IS `they have returned`
        `the day the person liable returned` IS `the day they returned`
        `the person's date of birth` IS `my date of birth`
        `the person was mentally incapable after it accrued` IS `I was mentally incapable`
        `the day the incapacity began` IS `the day the incapacity began`
        `the incapacity has ended` IS `the incapacity has ended`
        `the day the incapacity ended` IS `the day the incapacity ended`
        `the action survives for a deceased person's estate` IS `it is for an estate`
        `the day of the death` IS `the day of death`
        `the day of the grant of probate or administration` IS `the day of the grant`
        `a concerns notice was given` IS `a concerns notice was given`
        `the day the concerns notice was given` IS `the day of the concerns notice`

§§ `Abuse suffered as a child (Part 1A)`
-- Situation: you were abused as a child (under 18) and want damages for the injury, or for a death it caused.

@export Is there any time limit on my claim for damages for abuse I suffered as a child in South Australia (Limitation of Actions Act 1936 s 3A)?
GIVEN `the kind of abuse` IS A `Kind of abuse` @desc The kind of abuse: sexual abuse; serious physical abuse; psychological abuse related to sexual abuse or serious physical abuse; physical abuse that was not serious; psychological abuse not related to those; or another kind of abuse
      `my age when abused` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in completed years when the abuse happened (the youngest age, if it happened over a period)
GIVETH A `Child abuse answer`
`Is there a time limit on my child abuse claim` MEANS
    `the s 3A answer for` `the kind of abuse` `at age` `my age when abused`

@export My child abuse claim was barred by time before 1 February 2019, or an earlier action failed: can I sue now (Limitation of Actions Act 1936 s 3A; Limitation of Actions (Child Abuse) Amendment Act 2018 Sch 1 cll 2, 3)?
GIVEN `the kind of abuse` IS A `Kind of abuse` @desc The kind of abuse: sexual abuse; serious physical abuse; psychological abuse related to sexual abuse or serious physical abuse; physical abuse that was not serious; psychological abuse not related to those; or another kind of abuse
      `my age when abused` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in completed years when the abuse happened
      `the earlier proceedings` IS AN `Earlier proceedings on the claim` @desc What happened before on this claim: no earlier action or judgment; an action started but not finalised before 1 February 2019; an action started but discontinued before then; a judgment given because the limitation period had expired; or an action dismissed because the limitation period had expired
      `the court has granted permission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a court, satisfied that it is just and reasonable, has granted you permission to commence the action (needed only after a judgment or dismissal on the limitation ground)
GIVETH A `Previously barred answer`
`Can I sue now on my child abuse claim that was barred before` MEANS
    `the 2018 transitional answer` (`the s 3A answer for` `the kind of abuse` `at age` `my age when abused`) `the earlier proceedings` `the court has granted permission`

§§ `The time limit for my action (Parts 4 to 7)`

@export Which limitation period applies to my action in South Australia (Limitation of Actions Act 1936 ss 3A, 33-38)?
GIVEN `my kind of action` IS A `Kind of action` @desc The kind of action you would bring: damages for death or personal injury resulting from abuse suffered as a child (sexual, serious physical, or related psychological abuse); damages that include damages for personal injuries (any disease or impairment of physical or mental condition), in contract or tort; simple contract, tort, account or another s 35 action with no personal injury damages; defamation; recovery of money paid by mistake or on other restitutionary grounds; recovery of money paid as a tax that was invalid; rent under a lease by deed, or covenant or debt on a bond, other specialty, judgment or recognisance; money secured by a mortgage, judgment or lien or charged on land, or a legacy; or another kind of action
      `the day it accrued` IS A DATE @desc The day your cause of action accrued: for an injury, usually the day of the incident or exposure that caused it; for defamation, the day the matter was published (for electronic matter, first uploaded or sent); for an invalid tax, the day you paid it; for a judgment, the day it was recovered
      `my injury remained latent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a personal injury: whether the injury remained latent (unknown to you) for some time after its cause
GIVETH A `Period answer`
`Which limitation period applies to my action` MEANS
    `the period for` `my kind of action` `accrued on` `the day it accrued` `with latency` `my injury remained latent`

@export By when must I commence my action, counting the extensions for a latent injury, the defendant's absence, childhood or mental incapacity, an estate, and a defamation concerns notice (Limitation of Actions Act 1936 ss 3A, 33-39, 45, 46A)?
GIVEN `my kind of action` IS A `Kind of action` @desc The kind of action you would bring: damages for death or personal injury resulting from abuse suffered as a child (sexual, serious physical, or related psychological abuse); damages that include damages for personal injuries (any disease or impairment of physical or mental condition), in contract or tort; simple contract, tort, account or another s 35 action with no personal injury damages; defamation; recovery of money paid by mistake or on other restitutionary grounds; recovery of money paid as a tax that was invalid; rent under a lease by deed, or covenant or debt on a bond, other specialty, judgment or recognisance; money secured by a mortgage, judgment or lien or charged on land, or a legacy; or another kind of action
      `the day it accrued` IS A DATE @desc The day your cause of action accrued: for an injury, usually the day of the incident or exposure that caused it; for defamation, the day the matter was published (for electronic matter, first uploaded or sent); for an invalid tax, the day you paid it; for a judgment, the day it was recovered
      `my injury remained latent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a personal injury: whether the injury remained latent (unknown to you) for some time after its cause
      `the day I first knew of the injury` IS A DATE @desc For a latent injury: the day the injury first came to your knowledge (any day otherwise)
      `there was a later acknowledgment or payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a deed, bond, judgment, mortgage, charge or legacy: whether the person liable later acknowledged the debt in signed writing or paid part of the principal or interest
      `the day of the last acknowledgment or payment` IS A DATE @desc The day of the last such written acknowledgment or part payment (any day otherwise)
      `they were absent from the State` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a personal injury, contract or tort action: whether the person you would sue was absent from South Australia when the cause of action accrued
      `they have returned` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that person has since returned to South Australia
      `the day they returned` IS A DATE @desc The day that person returned to South Australia (any day if they were not absent or have not returned)
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth (you count as a child until your 18th birthday)
      `I was mentally incapable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, at some time since the cause of action accrued, a mental deficiency, disease or disorder made you incapable of reasoning or acting rationally about the action
      `the day the incapacity began` IS A DATE @desc The day that incapacity began (any day otherwise)
      `the incapacity has ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that incapacity has ended
      `the day the incapacity ended` IS A DATE @desc The day it ended (any day otherwise)
      `it is for an estate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you bring the action for the estate of a person who has died, the cause of action having survived for the estate's benefit
      `the day of death` IS A DATE @desc The day the person died (any day otherwise)
      `the day of the grant` IS A DATE @desc The day probate or letters of administration were granted to the executor or administrator (any day otherwise)
      `a concerns notice was given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For defamation: whether you gave the proposed defendant a concerns notice (as defined in the Defamation Act 2005)
      `the day of the concerns notice` IS A DATE @desc The day you gave the concerns notice (any day otherwise)
GIVETH A `Last day answer`
`By when must I commence my action` MEANS
    `the last day for` (`the facts from my answers` `my kind of action` `the day it accrued` `my injury remained latent` `the day I first knew of the injury` `there was a later acknowledgment or payment` `the day of the last acknowledgment or payment` `they were absent from the State` `they have returned` `the day they returned` `my date of birth` `I was mentally incapable` `the day the incapacity began` `the incapacity has ended` `the day the incapacity ended` `it is for an estate` `the day of death` `the day of the grant` `a concerns notice was given` `the day of the concerns notice`)

@export Was my action commenced in time, or am I still in time to commence it (Limitation of Actions Act 1936 ss 3A, 33-39, 45, 46A)?
GIVEN `my kind of action` IS A `Kind of action` @desc The kind of action you would bring: damages for death or personal injury resulting from abuse suffered as a child (sexual, serious physical, or related psychological abuse); damages that include damages for personal injuries (any disease or impairment of physical or mental condition), in contract or tort; simple contract, tort, account or another s 35 action with no personal injury damages; defamation; recovery of money paid by mistake or on other restitutionary grounds; recovery of money paid as a tax that was invalid; rent under a lease by deed, or covenant or debt on a bond, other specialty, judgment or recognisance; money secured by a mortgage, judgment or lien or charged on land, or a legacy; or another kind of action
      `the day it accrued` IS A DATE @desc The day your cause of action accrued: for an injury, usually the day of the incident or exposure that caused it; for defamation, the day the matter was published (for electronic matter, first uploaded or sent); for an invalid tax, the day you paid it; for a judgment, the day it was recovered
      `my injury remained latent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a personal injury: whether the injury remained latent (unknown to you) for some time after its cause
      `the day I first knew of the injury` IS A DATE @desc For a latent injury: the day the injury first came to your knowledge (any day otherwise)
      `there was a later acknowledgment or payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a deed, bond, judgment, mortgage, charge or legacy: whether the person liable later acknowledged the debt in signed writing or paid part of the principal or interest
      `the day of the last acknowledgment or payment` IS A DATE @desc The day of the last such written acknowledgment or part payment (any day otherwise)
      `they were absent from the State` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a personal injury, contract or tort action: whether the person you would sue was absent from South Australia when the cause of action accrued
      `they have returned` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that person has since returned to South Australia
      `the day they returned` IS A DATE @desc The day that person returned to South Australia (any day if they were not absent or have not returned)
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth (you count as a child until your 18th birthday)
      `I was mentally incapable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, at some time since the cause of action accrued, a mental deficiency, disease or disorder made you incapable of reasoning or acting rationally about the action
      `the day the incapacity began` IS A DATE @desc The day that incapacity began (any day otherwise)
      `the incapacity has ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that incapacity has ended
      `the day the incapacity ended` IS A DATE @desc The day it ended (any day otherwise)
      `it is for an estate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you bring the action for the estate of a person who has died, the cause of action having survived for the estate's benefit
      `the day of death` IS A DATE @desc The day the person died (any day otherwise)
      `the day of the grant` IS A DATE @desc The day probate or letters of administration were granted to the executor or administrator (any day otherwise)
      `a concerns notice was given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For defamation: whether you gave the proposed defendant a concerns notice (as defined in the Defamation Act 2005)
      `the day of the concerns notice` IS A DATE @desc The day you gave the concerns notice (any day otherwise)
      `I have commenced it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have commenced (filed) the action
      `the day I commenced it` IS A DATE @desc The day you commenced it (any day if you have not)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
GIVETH A `Time limit answer`
`Was my action commenced in time` MEANS
    `was the action commenced in time` (`the facts from my answers` `my kind of action` `the day it accrued` `my injury remained latent` `the day I first knew of the injury` `there was a later acknowledgment or payment` `the day of the last acknowledgment or payment` `they were absent from the State` `they have returned` `the day they returned` `my date of birth` `I was mentally incapable` `the day the incapacity began` `the incapacity has ended` `the day the incapacity ended` `it is for an estate` `the day of death` `the day of the grant` `a concerns notice was given` `the day of the concerns notice`) `I have commenced it` `the day I commenced it` `today`

@export Do I get more time to sue because I was out of South Australia or in prison (Limitation of Actions Act 1936 s 46)?
GIVEN `the reason` IS A `Reason for more time` @desc Why you want more time: you were absent from the State, or you were imprisoned
GIVETH AN `Absence answer`
`Do I get more time because I was away or in prison` MEANS
    `the s 46 answer` `the reason`

§§ `Defamation (ss 37A, 37B)`
-- Situation: you were defamed and want to sue.

@export The same defamatory matter was published again: from when does my time to sue over the later publication run (Limitation of Actions Act 1936 s 37A)?
GIVEN `the first publication day` IS A DATE @desc The day the matter was first published (for electronic matter, the day it was first uploaded or sent)
      `the first was to the public` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the first publication was to the public, or a section of the public
      `the later publication day` IS A DATE @desc The day of the later publication you would sue over
      `the later publisher` IS A `Later publisher` @desc Who made the later publication: the first publisher; its employee; its contractor publishing as such; an associated entity of it (Corporations Act 2001 s 50AAA) or that entity's employee or contractor; or someone else
      `it is substantially the same matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the later matter is substantially the same as the first
      `the court finds the manner materially different` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court finds the manner of the later publication materially different from the first (for example in prominence or extent)
GIVETH A `Single publication answer`
`From when does my time run for a later publication` MEANS
    `the s 37A answer` `the first publication day` `the first was to the public` `the later publication day` `the later publisher` `it is substantially the same matter` `the court finds the manner materially different`

@export Can the court extend my one-year time limit for a defamation action, and to when (Limitation of Actions Act 1936 s 37B)?
GIVEN `the publication day` IS A DATE @desc The day of the publication you sue over (for a republication covered by s 37A, the first publication)
      `I can satisfy the court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you can satisfy the court that it is just and reasonable to allow your action to proceed (it looks at the length of and reasons for your delay, when you learnt the facts, and lost evidence)
GIVETH A `Defamation extension answer`
`Can the court extend my defamation time limit` MEANS
    `the s 37B answer` `the publication day` `I can satisfy the court`

§§ `Short time limits, extensions and notices (ss 47, 48, 50)`

@export Another law gives me less than 12 months to sue: do I still have 12 months (Limitation of Actions Act 1936 s 47)?
GIVEN `the day it arose` IS A DATE @desc The day your cause of action arose
      `the last day the other law allows` IS A DATE @desc The last day the other Act, regulation, rule or by-law allows for bringing the action
      `the kind of proceeding` IS AN `Excepted action` @desc Whether the action is one of these: a criminal action; an action to try the validity of an election or of title to an office; an action to try the validity of a local government assessment, rate or loan; or none of these
      `the court thinks the limit essential` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court is of the opinion that the short limit is essential to the nature or purpose of the action
GIVETH A `Twelve months answer`
`Do I still have 12 months to sue` MEANS
    `the s 47 answer` `the day it arose` `the last day the other law allows` `the kind of proceeding` `the court thinks the limit essential`

@export Can the court extend the time for my action after the time limit has passed (Limitation of Actions Act 1936 s 48)?
GIVEN `the time limit` IS A `Whose time limit` @desc Which time limit you missed or will miss: a limitation period in the Limitation of Actions Act 1936 (other than for an invalid tax); the period for recovering an invalid tax (s 38(2)); or a time limit in another Act, regulation, rule or by-law
      `it is criminal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the proceeding is a criminal proceeding
      `I learnt a material fact late` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether there is a fact you learnt late that forms an essential element of your cause of action or would have major significance on an assessment of your loss (for an injury: a substantial reduction of capacity to work, much more medical care, or a significant loss of expectation of life)
      `the day I learnt it` IS A DATE @desc The day you ascertained that fact (any day otherwise)
      `the last day of my period` IS A DATE @desc The last day of the limitation period you missed (from the question "By when must I commence my action")
      `the day I commence` IS A DATE @desc The day you commenced, or will commence, the action
      `the defendant's conduct caused my reasonable delay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you failed to sue in time because of representations or conduct of the defendant (or someone you reasonably believed was acting for them), and your failure was reasonable in view of them
      `the court finds it just` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court is satisfied that in all the circumstances it is just to extend time (it looks at prejudice to a fair trial, finality, your loss and both sides' conduct)
GIVETH AN `Extension answer`
`Can the court extend my time` MEANS
    `the s 48 answer` `the time limit` `it is criminal` `I learnt a material fact late` `the day I learnt it` `the last day of my period` `the day I commence` `the defendant's conduct caused my reasonable delay` `the court finds it just`

@export I did not give a notice that a law requires before suing: can the court excuse it (Limitation of Actions Act 1936 s 50)?
GIVEN `a law requires notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an Act, regulation, rule or by-law requires you to give notice of your intention to sue, or of your claim, before the action is instituted
      `justice requires it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court finds that the justice of the case requires dispensing with the notice
GIVETH A `Dispensation answer`
`Can the court excuse my notice before action` MEANS
    `the s 50 answer` `a law requires notice` `justice requires it`

§§ `An injury suffered as a child: notice of the intended action (s 45A)`
-- Situation: you suffered a personal injury while under 18.

@export I was injured as a child: must I give notice of my intended action, to whom, and by when (Limitation of Actions Act 1936 s 45A(1), (2))?
GIVEN `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth
      `the day of the incident` IS A DATE @desc The day of the incident out of which the injury arose
      `it resulted from child abuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injury resulted from sexual or serious physical abuse (or related psychological abuse) suffered as a child
      `it arose from an intentional tort` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injury arose from an intentional tort (for example an assault)
      `I sue the person who committed it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your action is against the person who actually committed that intentional tort
      `someone else is alleged to be liable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether any other person (for example an employer) is alleged to be liable for it
      `it arose out of a motor accident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injury is alleged to have arisen out of a motor accident
GIVETH A `Notice answer`
`Must I give notice of my intended action` MEANS
    `the s 45A(1) notice answer` `my date of birth` `the day of the incident` `it resulted from child abuse` `it arose from an intentional tort` `I sue the person who committed it` `someone else is alleged to be liable` `it arose out of a motor accident`

@export Was my notice of intended action given within 6 years after the incident, or is there still time (Limitation of Actions Act 1936 s 45A(1))?
GIVEN `the day of the incident` IS A DATE @desc The day of the incident out of which the injury arose
      `I have given it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether notice of the intended action has been given (by you or on your behalf)
      `the day I gave it` IS A DATE @desc The day it was given (any day if not)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
GIVETH A `Time limit answer`
`Was my notice of intended action in time` MEANS
    `was the s 45A notice given in time` `the day of the incident` `I have given it` `the day I gave it` `today`

@export The defendant gave me written notice requiring me to sue: by when must I bring the action (Limitation of Actions Act 1936 s 45A(5))?
GIVEN `the day of their notice` IS A DATE @desc The date of the defendant's written notice requiring you to bring an action
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I sue after the defendant's notice` MEANS
    `the last day to sue after the defendant's notice of` `the day of their notice`

@export Did I bring my action within 6 months after the defendant's notice, or is there still time (Limitation of Actions Act 1936 s 45A(5))?
GIVEN `the day of their notice` IS A DATE @desc The date of the defendant's written notice requiring you to bring an action
      `I have brought it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have brought the action
      `the day I brought it` IS A DATE @desc The day you brought it (any day if not)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
GIVETH A `Time limit answer`
`Did I sue in time after the defendant's notice` MEANS
    `was the action brought in time after the defendant's notice` `the day of their notice` `I have brought it` `the day I brought it` `today`

@export What do I lose if I did not comply with the notice, records, examination or 6-month requirements for a child's injury claim (Limitation of Actions Act 1936 s 45A(7))?
GIVEN `I complied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you complied with every requirement of s 45A that applied to you (notice within 6 years; giving records or attending a medical examination on the defendant's reasonable request; suing within 6 months of the defendant's notice)
      `the court excuses it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court is satisfied that there is good reason to excuse the non-compliance
GIVETH A `Non-compliance answer`
`What do I lose for not complying with s 45A` MEANS
    `the s 45A(7) answer` `I complied` `the court excuses it`

§§ `Recovering a tax that was invalid (s 38(2)-(3b))`
-- Situation: you paid a tax, fee or charge that turned out to be invalid.

@export How much of the invalid tax I paid can I recover, given the windfall rule (Limitation of Actions Act 1936 s 38(3a), (3b))?
GIVEN `the amount I paid` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount you paid as the tax, fee or charge, in dollars (not counting any part that would have been an overpayment even if it had been valid)
      `the amount I passed on` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of the burden of that payment you passed on to other people (for example in your prices), in dollars
      `the amount I paid back` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of the amount passed on you have paid back, or entered into an enforceable agreement to pay back, in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much of the invalid tax can I recover` MEANS
    `the invalid tax recoverable from` `the amount I paid` `passed on` `the amount I passed on` `paid back` `the amount I paid back`
